Subject: [PATCH] spi: geni-qcom: log GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO on QSPI controllers

prep_se_for_gpi_dma() matches qcspi8380.sys register for register, but
Windows skips that whole block when GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO bit 0
(FIFO_IF_DISABLE) is set, while we always write it before each message.
Whether the difference matters depends on the bit's value on these
serial engines, which is not known. Log it once per QSPI controller at
probe. Behaviour is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index dea5b1668..ca589fa0a 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -861,8 +861,15 @@ static int spi_geni_init(struct spi_geni_master *mas)
 	 * regardless of what GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO reports.
 	 */
 	fifo_disable = readl(se->base + GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO) & FIFO_IF_DISABLE;
-	if (spi_geni_is_qspi(mas))
+	if (spi_geni_is_qspi(mas)) {
+		/*
+		 * qcspi8380.sys skips its GPI register setup when this bit is
+		 * set; record it so that difference can be judged on hardware.
+		 */
+		dev_info(mas->dev, "QSPI GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO FIFO_IF_DISABLE=%u\n",
+			 fifo_disable);
 		fifo_disable = 1;
+	}
 
 	switch (fifo_disable) {
 	case 1:
